L148: Use the link below to share a full-text version of this article with your friends and colleagues. 【17†Learn more.】\nL149: \nL150: [Button: Copy URL]\nL151: \nL152: Share a link\nL153: \nL154: Share on\nL155: ### Graphical Abstract\nL156: \nL157: In a parallel universe: DNA origami structures based on modified parallel double-crossover tiles (see scheme) were constructed and a unidirectional (parallel) arrangement of the scaffold strand (gray lines) was used in the assembly of a variety of 2D and 3D DNA origami structures. This will greatly expand the diversity of DNA origami and enable their assembly into larger structures.\nL158: ##\nL159: \nL160: Supporting Information\nL161: \nL162: As a service to our authors and readers, this journal provides supporting information supplied by the authors. Such materials are peer reviewed and may be re-organized for online delivery, but are not copy-edited or typeset. Technical support issues arising from supporting information (other than missing files) should be addressed to the authors.\nL163: \nL164: Filename  | Description\nL165: --- | ---\nL166: 【18†anie_201302177_sm_miscellaneous_information.pdf】25.1 MB  | miscellaneous_information\nL167: Please note: The publisher is not responsible for the content or functionality of any supporting information supplied by the authors. Any queries (other than missing content) should be directed to the corresponding author for the article.\nL168: ## 【15†References】\nL169: \nL170:   * 1 T. J. Fu, N. C. Seeman, Biochemistry 1993, 32, 3211–3220.\nL171: \nL172: 【19†CAS】 【20†PubMed】 【21†Web of Science®】 【22†Google Scholar】\nL173: \nL174:   * 2 E. Winfree, F. Liu, L. A. Wenzler, N. C. Seeman, Nature 1998, 394, 539–544.\nL175: \nL176: 【23†CAS】 【24†PubMed】 【25†Web of Science®】 【26†Google Scholar】\nL177: \nL178:   * 3 P. W. K. Rothemund, N. Papadakis, E. Winfree, PLoS Biol. 2004, 2, e 424.\nL179: \nL180: 【27†PubMed】 【28†Web of Science®】 【29†Google Scholar】\nL181: \nL182:   * 4 F. Mathieu et